canfield -- Canfield solitaire (the casino game)================================================    canfieldCanfield is the solitaire the casinos took a cut of: you pay to start adeck and earn back a few units for every card you work up to a foundation,so the score is money.  Cards build down in alternating colours on thetableau and up by suit on the foundations; spaces are filled from thestock, and `ht' deals a fresh row from the hand to the talon.You name a move by the two things it joins -- `s2' stock to tableau 2,`tf' talon to a foundation, `13' tableau 1 to tableau 3, `2f' tableau 2 toa foundation.  `c' toggles card counting, `b' shows your betting position,`q' ends the game.4.3BSD Net/2, from The Unix Heritage Society's archive.  A running accountis kept in GAMES/cfscores when that file is present.  Full originals inSRC/canfield/ORIG.